Z||000000||1FST2M6||02-27-2000||01:58 AM||||I haven't done anything internal to my motor with the exception of valves. Ported the throttle body, had Extrude hone do the upper and lower intake. added injectors and a chip, K&N, Flowmaster. I hoped in a friends Fiero (86 GT 4spd) he's a member in the forum  BlackGT  What a lethargic dog. (sorry todd) I've pointed him down what I think to be the right path twards gobs of GO. Upon driving his car I asked another fiero owner if i may take his car for a spin... Again  87 V6 5spd. (some mods) Again, Not even close to what i'm used to... I've even Raced a fellow owner at Atlanta International Dragway (BEFORE i had the injector upgrade or the nitrous) I pulled him by more than a second in the 1/4. Is there a BIG difference in weight between the SE and the GT? I have an 86 SE. What gives? Serious question! I'm trying to help BlackGT out but if there is a big difference what is it? My car has 95k on it and his 110K both 4spd. ANd his motor is actully fresh (under 10k) All he says when he dirves my car is "I WANT THIS.." Now i know why but is there a good explination to its lack of go...  It idles fine get decent gas mileage.. Looks SWEET (Fastback... of course) Just wish i knew what to tell him. I'm not sure of any other mods to his car other than a recent rebuild. He is out of town till sunday night I'll make sure he gets on here and lets the rest of you know... ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phaeton||02-27-2000||01:18 PM||||Lets see, new injectors make more fuel available, new chip puts that fuel in cylinder at WOT then lights it sooner, increasing cylinder pressures. Airflow mods get the gasses in and out more efficiently.  Looks to kick but on an unmodified engine, even a new one.<BR>What was the question? it's early and I need coffee.  <BR>Big difference? I feel that optimizing everthing to what it was designed to be is a big difference over what got put together on an assembly line by someone who didn't care.<P>Then again maybe the other Fieros were out of tune and their throttle cables are too long. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000002||Raydar||02-27-2000||02:39 PM||||Travis... I think the GT is just a bit heavier than the SE. Hasn't your car been lightened? AC, and spare tire removed, etc.?||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||02-27-2000||04:42 PM||||I'm not sure what the difference is, but it's very minimal in terms of weight.  Mechanically, it should be basically the same. Same hp and tq ratings... 10 lbs roughly translates to 1 hp according to a racing site I had visited. Are you certain his car is not out of tune?  Before you modded your car, what was it like in comparision?  Also, see what gears he's running.||||reg||14
Z||000004||1FST2M6||02-27-2000||06:00 PM||||BlackGTs car now has Jamex spring and some strange acting monroe Sensa-trac.. not sure if i like them.. but it's not my car to say...   ok.. Well before i had anything really done.. (the day i bought the car it got a dyno run, K&N, Throttle body bypass, NGK UR5 plugs, no resonator box and a High flow cat all the same day) But my car compared to the other 2 i have driven just seem uum.. lethargic isn't a decent word.. almost unwilling to rev. you stab the gas and mine LEAPS to 4 grand.. stand on the other and it takes a considerably longer. Same 4spd and a fresher motor. But their is no major weight issue.... humm i'm lost.. I want to give Todd (BlackGT) what he wants a replica of my go and his fastback looks but his car just doesn't seem willing to, or just would rather cruise around than get FLOGGED! humm.. well if any of you think of any thing that i can do different to his car help us out! Today i put the Jamex spring, shocks/struts Throttle body bypass... he's on his way... thanks for all your help! I'll let ya know what he thinks... ||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT Bastard||02-27-2000||08:23 PM||||How long have you had your car?  Are you 100% sure that the previous owner didn't change anything? There must be some sort of casting #'s on the engine block.  It might be intersting to see if your car was the subject of a 3.1 stroker or 3.4 build-up.  It's worth checking.||||reg||1
Z||000006||BlackGT||02-28-2000||09:45 PM||||Hey Guys,<BR>Travis is right....compared to his fast 2m6<BR>my GT is a dog! Ya heard me! But it looks cool thanks to his efforts over the weekend.<BR>The first thing that needs to be done is to<BR>replace that friggin clutch(excuse the french!) What good is getting a new rebuilt <BR>engine installed and then have another stock<BR>clutch put in.....what a piece of crap! The<BR>clutch that Travis uses in his car is the<BR>one I`ll get for mine. We were talking last<BR>nite and he thinks that the rear main seal<BR>has contaminated the clutch. The cost of a new rear seal is peanuts so I`ll get that<BR>this week if I can along with a 4 puck clutch<BR>so I can at least feel the Horsepower I`ve<BR>already paid for. If you guys and gals are<BR>fortunate enough to have a Fiero Club in your<BR>town you should get involved, If I had not met this bunch of folks not only would I be<BR>spending a fortune trying to repair my baby<BR>but would have no way of knowing how much<BR>potential these cars really have....once again Trav THANKS!!!<P>      BlackGT<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||02-28-2000||11:22 PM||||Sure any time Todd. I've got that spare 4 puck sitting here.. Still trying to con Ed into letting me have a lift all weekend.. I'll let ya know. You need a quick car... So i have somthing else to play with when you go out of town...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">     As for the 3.1 upgrade. unfortunatly no. I bought the car from its original owner have all his documentation window sticker and canceled check. The other owner was an Attorney in the metro atlanta area (Tucker) and drove it 6 miles to work when it was nice out the rest of the time he drove either this SWEET Volvo P 1800 S  or the Volvo 240D  I guess he was into saftey... I should call him and ask him if he wants too see it now... hummmmm||||reg||10
